{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:ClimaxVolumeMass.VertexAlgebraJetRelations","@type":"LeanModule","name":"ClimaxVolumeMass.VertexAlgebraJetRelations","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.HeckeGS","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.descent_idempotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.descent_idempotent","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-jet-relations.lean#L178-L193","doc":"D-4: The descent involution τ̂_n = ℓ_n ∘ 𝔡_{n+1} is idempotent.\nThis splits the algebra into descended (bosonic) and transient\n(fermionic) parts.\n\nProof: τ̂² = (ℓ ∘ 𝔡) ∘ (ℓ ∘ 𝔡) = ℓ ∘ (𝔡 ∘ ℓ) ∘ 𝔡 = ℓ ∘ id ∘ 𝔡 = ℓ ∘ 𝔡 = τ̂. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.DescentOperator.descent_left_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.DescentOperator.descent_left_inv","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-jet-relations.lean#L176-L176","doc":"The key identity: 𝔡 ∘ ℓ = id. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.DescentOperator.descent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.DescentOperator.descent","kind":"def","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-jet-relations.lean#L174-L174","doc":"The descent homomorphism 𝔡_{n+1} : H^{(n+1)} → H^{(n)}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.DescentOperator.jet_embed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.DescentOperator.jet_embed","kind":"def","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-jet-relations.lean#L172-L172","doc":"The jet prolongation ℓ_n : H^{(n)} → H^{(n+1)}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.DescentOperator.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.DescentOperator.mk","kind":"ctor","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-jet-relations.lean#L170-L170","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.DescentOperator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.DescentOperator","kind":"structure","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-jet-relations.lean#L165-L176","doc":"The descent operator τ̂_n = ℓ_n ∘ 𝔡_{n+1} on the Hecke algebra\nat brane level n.  Built from jet prolongation ℓ_n and descent\nhomomorphism 𝔡_{n+1}.  This is a specific operator, not an\narbitrary endomorphism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.yekutieli_coeff_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.yekutieli_coeff_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-jet-relations.lean#L141-L159","doc":"JC-4: The Yekutieli obstruction κ_n measures the transient part\nof the R-matrix at level n+1:\nκ_n = tr_M^{(n+1)}((1 - τ̂_n) Ř^{(n+1)}).\n\n**Re-scoped 2026-11-15 (owner decision, PR #7747).** This block used to\ncarry `axiom yekutieli_perpetual`, documented as \"κ_n ≠ 0 for all n when\nχ = -6\" but stating only `q > 1 → q⁻¹(1 - q⁻¹) ≠ 0`. That statement is the\ntheorem below, so the axiom was removed (it had no consumers). The\ndocumented claim is also withdrawn: on Bring's surface the jet obstruction\nvanishes exactly when `n ∣ χ = -6`, i.e. for `n ∈ {1, 2, 3, 6}`, and\npersists for `n ∤ 6` (item 3 of `thm:qu-to-qou`, bean `qou-lx8f`). What is\nproved here is only that the coefficient `q⁻¹(1 - q⁻¹)` is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.euler_level_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.euler_level_stable","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-jet-relations.lean#L123-L135","doc":"JC-3: χ(A_n) = χ(A_0) = -6 for all brane levels n.\nThe rigidity trace of the identity is level-invariant.\n\n**Restated 2026-09-04.** This was `theorem euler_level_stable (_n : ℕ) :\n(2 : ℤ) - 2 * 4 = -6 := by norm_num` — a `norm_num` arithmetic fact that\nmentions no brane level and would hold if the numbers came from anywhere\nelse, under a docstring about level-invariance. It now names `eulerChar`\nand states both halves of the claim, so it is false if `eulerChar` is\nwrong or level-sensitive. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:vertex-algebra-jet-relations","label":"prop:vertex-algebra-jet-relations","md":"quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-jet-relations.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.eulerChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.eulerChar","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-jet-relations.lean#L114-L121","doc":"The Euler characteristic of the level-`n` brane algebra, `χ = 2 - 2g`\nat genus `g = 4`.\n\nStated as a function of the level so that the stability theorem below\nsays something about it. The level is discarded — that is the content\nbeing recorded, and writing it out is what makes the theorem falsifiable\nrather than an arithmetic identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.levelHecke_succ_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.levelHecke_succ_eq","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-jet-relations.lean#L82-L108","doc":"J-3c, in the form the Lean actually supports.\n\nThe claim this section is *about*: the Markov trace is level-independent\non descended elements, `tr_M^{(n+1)}(ℓ_n(w)) = tr_M^{(n)}(w)` for all\n`w ∈ H^{(n)}(q)` — the knot-coordinate form of Euler characteristic\nstability, i.e. the Jones polynomial of a knot does not depend on brane\nlevel.\n\n**This was a bare `axiom`, and it is provable — by `rfl`.** Its statement is\n`levelHecke hp n level = levelHecke hp n (level + 1)`, and `levelHecke`\ndiscards its level argument, so both sides are the same term. Assuming it\nbought nothing, while adding a global axiom to `#print axioms` for every\nstatement downstream.\n\n**What it does NOT establish is what its docstring claimed.** That text read\n\"the Markov trace is level-independent on descended elements,\n`tr_M^{(n+1)}(ℓ_n(w)) = tr_M^{(n)}(w)`\" — a claim about the Markov trace and\nthe jet embedding. Neither appears in the statement, and the bound\n`w : AlgElement (HeckeGen n) ℝ` was never used, which is the tell. The real\nclaim needs `tr_M` and `ℓ_n` formalised; it is not in this file and is not\nproved anywhere by this declaration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.hecke_level_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.hecke_level_independent","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-jet-relations.lean#L55-L76","doc":"J-1: The Hecke relation at level n has the same form as at level 0.\nThe substrate parameter q does not depend on the brane level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.levelHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.JetRelations.levelHecke","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-jet-relations.lean#L41-L49","doc":"The Hecke algebra at brane level n is H_{k}(q) where k is the\nstrand count. The substrate parameter q is the same at every level\n(Euler characteristic stability). ","signatureChunk":0}]}